      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Hey team! I've got a quick memo draft for you, but before we send it out, I need to make sure you've got a few extra \"goblets\" of information ready, just in case some of our remote staff are feeling a bit goblin-like and need a little extra help.\n\nHere is the draft, but I've added a few little goblin notes to keep things interesting:\n\n***\n\n**Subject: Keeping Our Workstations Comfortable (and Avoiding the Goblin Grip)**\n\nHi everyone,\n\nAs we continue to work from our homes, I wanted to take a moment to remind you about the importance of ergonomics. We want to make sure you can focus on your work without worrying about aches and pains, especially in your wrists and back.\n\n**A Few Quick Tips:**\n*   **Chair Height:** Adjust your chair so your feet rest flat on the floor (or on a footrest if your legs are too long). Your knees should be at a 90-degree angle.\n*   **Monitor Level:** The top of your screen should be at or slightly below eye level. This helps prevent neck strain.\n*   **Wrist Position:** Keep your wrists straight while typing",
      "source": "target",
