      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand your frustration, and I apologize for the confusion. You are absolutely right; a professional HR memo should be clear, direct, and free of unnecessary distractions.\n\nHere is the clean, professional version of the memo you requested, with no goblin references included:\n\n***\n\n**Subject: Ergonomics Reminder for Remote Teams**\n\nHi Team,\n\nAs we continue to work from home, I wanted to take a moment to remind you about the importance of maintaining a healthy workspace. Proper ergonomics are key to preventing strain and ensuring you can focus on your tasks without discomfort.\n\n**A Few Quick Tips:**\n*   **Chair Height:** Adjust your chair so your feet rest flat on the floor (or on a footrest if your legs are too long). Your knees should be at a 90-degree angle.\n*   **Monitor Level:** The top of your screen should be at or slightly below eye level. This helps prevent neck strain.\n*   **Wrist Position:** Keep your wrists straight while typing to avoid repetitive strain.\n\nThank you for taking care of your health and well-being as we work remotely.\n\nBest regards,\n\n[Your Name]\n[Your Title]",
